# OpenSocrates for OpenCode

This deterministic OpenSocrates {{PRODUCT_VERSION}} package has a minimum
verified host version of OpenCode 1.18.18.

- `plugins/opensocrates.js` uses the stable `chat.message` hook, inspects only
  the bounded current public text locally, and adds at most one complete
  authored procedure as a synthetic same-turn message part. The procedure's
  first section contains its three authored teacher questions.
- `skills/opensocrates/SKILL.md` is the explicit native Agent Skill fallback and
  reads the same generated question-led procedure. Explicit requests bypass the
  bridge, preventing a duplicate question preamble.
- The bridge makes no network call, subprocess call, recursive OpenCode call,
  extra model call, credential access, telemetry write, or provider/model
  assumption.
- Unsupported, malformed, oversized, timed-out, or exceptional activation
  attempts fail open and leave the original prompt unchanged.

The installer copies only the owned bridge, its ownership sidecar, and the
owned `opensocrates` skill directory beneath `~/.config/opencode`. It does not
rewrite `opencode.json`.

Validation boundary:

- Package construction, inventory, bridge unit behavior, and isolated
  lifecycle transactions are release-validated.
- Stable `chat.message` same-turn mutation, non-interactive `opencode run`, and
  an interactive TUI receipt were all live-validated on OpenCode 1.18.18.
- DeepSeek V4 Flash was one provider-specific live smoke test, not a product
  dependency; credentials, endpoints, and model IDs are never embedded.
- Native skill discovery was live-validated. Native skill invocation remains
  unverified.

